12:25:17 SQL> -- Description:
12:25:17 SQL> --   Purges PS_* history rows matched via PSARCH tables within a date window.
12:25:17 SQL> --   TEST MODE: Uses ROLLBACK in place of COMMIT (see inline comments).
12:25:17 SQL> -- **********************************************************************
12:25:17 SQL> -- Note: RUN AS SYSADM
12:25:17 SQL> -- HISTORY:
12:25:17 SQL> -- 2025-12-25  Anandmohan Singh  SQL*Plus refactor; test-mode rollbacks
12:25:17 SQL> -- 2026-01-06  Linux-friendly; runtime prompts; no default target DB
12:25:17 SQL> -- **********************************************************************
12:25:17 SQL> 
12:25:17 SQL> -- =========[ Runtime Parameters via command line ]=========
12:25:17 SQL> -- Usage:
12:25:17 SQL> --   sqlplus sysadm/*******@SERVICE @export_delete_script_final6.SQL <DB_NAME> <START_DATE> <END_DATE>
12:25:17 SQL> -- Example:
12:25:17 SQL> --   sqlplus sysadm/*******@FSSNDX    @export_delete_script_final6.SQL FSSNDX 2025-12-01 2025-12-31
12:25:17 SQL> -- Notes:
12:25:17 SQL> --   Dates must be YYYY-MM-DD. End date is inclusive.
12:25:17 SQL> --   Parameter positions: &1=DB_NAME, &2=START_DATE, &3=END_DATE
12:25:17 SQL> 
12:25:17 SQL> -- Map positional parameters to named defines (so the rest of the block stays untouched)
12:25:17 SQL> define p_target_db = '&1'
